How does this work?
Suppose a hacker wants to check the open ports in a system. He continually checks for open ports by sending packets. What the IDS sees:

                        Port scanned 1, Ports scanned 2, then 3, 4..... up to 100 ports scanned in a very short time.
                                                                      
                                                                  |
                                      
                                Informed the administrator of this unknown behaviour and generated alerts
                    
                                                                  |

                                                The attack continues until someone stops it. 


Types of IDS: 
There are mainly two types of IDS:
1. Host IDS: A system that works for only a single host. It is installed on specialised systems, such as server computers, monitoring systems, and host computers. We can view the running processes, check the system log, and so on.  
2. Network IDS (NIDS): An intrusion detection system that is used to monitor the whole network. It can detect unauthorised access, malicious activities, and attempts to scan the network, among other things. It can just detect and inform the administrator. 
